Fixed all 10 failures across the three modules; `pytest -q` now reports **15 passed**.

What was wrong:

- **`src/auth.py`** — `has_permission` compared roles case-sensitively; `is_admin_or_owner` used `and` instead of the documented `or` (owner or admin alone must grant access).
- **`src/inventory.py`** — mutable default `{}` shared stock between instances; `add` overwrote the SKU instead of accumulating; `reserve` used `>=` so reserving exactly the available stock raised `OutOfStock`; `release` never raised when releasing more than reserved.
- **`src/text_utils.py`** — `slugify` didn't lowercase and only collapsed double hyphens (so `hello   world!!!` → `hello--world`), now collapses runs in one pass; `truncate` appended the suffix on top of `max_len` characters instead of reserving room for it.

No changes under `tests/`.
